BT /F1 16 Tf 72 720 Td (Chapter Three. The Trial Balance) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 90 690 Td (At the end of a period the clerk lists every account with its balance, debits in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 676 Td (one column and credits in the other. This list is the trial balance, and the two) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 662 Td (columns must add to the same total.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 90 648 Td (If they do not, the search begins. A difference divisible by nine suggests two) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 634 Td (digits transposed; a difference equal to a single entry suggests a posting made to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 620 Td (one side only; a difference twice an entry suggests a posting made to the wrong side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 90 606 Td (When the trial balance agrees, the adjustments are made, and a second trial) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 592 Td (balance is drawn up after them. From this adjusted list the statements of the period) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 578 Td (are prepared.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 90 564 Td (The trial balance is a working paper, not a report. It is seldom shown to anyone) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 550 Td (outside the office, but it is the bridge between the books and the statements, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 536 Td (every figure in the statements can be traced back across it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 302 50 Td (4) Tj ET
